            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, justice Alito questioned whether extending a lifeline to the government concedes that the loss amount is not an element of the offense."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9e21b2335b17ecd78011cd230ca973f55890f5a7a2fd7db10f90a12c41ce4192",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9e21b2335b17-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito asked whether there is authority for a trial judge to ask a jury a special interrogatory about immigration status in tax cases."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9e21b2335b17ecd78011cd230ca973f55890f5a7a2fd7db10f90a12c41ce4192",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9e21b2335b17-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy, justice Kennedy noted that multiple defendants might find a special interrogatory unnecessary or inflammatory."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9e21b2335b17ecd78011cd230ca973f55890f5a7a2fd7db10f90a12c41ce4192",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9e21b2335b17-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 26,
              "start": 26
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked why the government would be reluctant to use a special interrogatory."
      }
